    {
      "id": "Measure 9-185",
      "title": "Establishes Five Deschutes County Commissioner Districts",
      "summary": "Deschutes County Commissioners are now elected countywide, so every voter can vote for all five Commissioner positions. This measure would, beginning with the 2028 election, elect one Commissioner from each of five geographic districts shown on the measure's map, and voters could vote only for the Commissioner of their own district. Candidates would have to be registered to vote in, and have lived for one year in, the district they seek to represent.",
      "yesMeans": "Starting in 2028, each Commissioner would be elected by and from one of five geographic districts.",
